	(text "Classic 5.8 GHz analog VTX uses wideband FM for video and adds an audio subcarrier (commonly ~6.5 MHz) FM-modulated by your mic line. Your cam's AUDIO pin (or an external mic board) goes to VTX AUDIO IN through an AC-coupling cap (1 µF-4.7 µF), sometimes with a small series resistor (e.g., 1 k-10 k) per the VTX datasheet. (This mirrors TV subcarrier practice; exact frequency is VTX-specific.)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 518.16 107.95 0)
